/F2 22 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 274 Tm (Keeping a Fire) Tj
/F3 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 243 Tm (A short guide for a cold evening) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 213 Tm (Lay the fire before you need it. Start with a bed of ash, then a) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 193 Tm (handful of dry kindling, then two split logs leaning together so) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 173 Tm (air can move between them. Light the kindling, not the logs.) Tj
/F2 14 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 143 Tm (Tending the hearth) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 120 Tm (A good fire needs little help once it catches. Add one log at a) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 100 Tm (time, and only when the last one has burned down to glowing coals.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 80 Tm (Keep the screen in front of the fire whenever you leave the room.) Tj
ET
endstream
